{"conversation_id":"d1ccc40d-4dc7-4e56-a262-4f3b5a29838d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### TDD GREEN Summary\n\n**Test Counts**: 103/103 passed across 10 test files (0 failures). `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n\n---\n\n### Root-Cause Analysis\n\n- **D1 (Qualified-Name Resolvability)**: [`findCommand`](file:///home/bhd/Documents/Projects/bhd/cmd-pallet/src/catalog.ts#L120-L150) previously stripped only leading slashes and matched strictly against unqualified command names (`c.name`), causing scope-qualified lookup queries like `claude:dup-command` to fail candidate resolution.\n- **D2 (Exit-Code Propagation)**: [`bin/cmd-pallet.js`](file:///home/bhd/Documents/Projects/bhd/cmd-pallet/bin/cmd-pallet.js#L13-L31) and [`src/cli.ts`](file:///home/bhd/Documents/Projects/bhd/cmd-pallet/src/cli.ts#L18-L23) did not invoke `runCli` or propagate its return code to `process.exit(code)` / `process.exitCode` when launched in stripped-types execution mode, causing binary invocations to exit prematurely with default `0` and empty stdout.\n- **D3 (Search \u0026 List Output Deduplication)**: [`dispatch`](file:///home/bhd/Documents/Projects/bhd/cmd-pallet/src/dispatch.ts#L106-L125) emitted all command matches across all agent configurations and scopes without deduplication, allowing identical command names across multiple scopes to produce redundant lines and JSON entries.\n\n---\n\n### Verification \u0026 Push\n\n- **Commit**: `fix: qualified-name resolution, exit codes, output dedup (3 live defects)` ([`653924a`](https://github.com/buihongduc132/cmd-pallet/commit/653924a))\n- **Remote**: Pushed to `origin/main`\n","duration_seconds":878.917183573,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":335656,"output_tokens":34986,"thinking_tokens":27375,"cache_read_tokens":5588054,"total_tokens":370642}}
